{number: 142}
{title: Nearer, Still Nearer}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Nearer, still nearer, [F] close to Thy [C] heart,
Draw me, my Savior, so [G7] precious Thou [C] art;
Fold me, O [F] fold me [C] close to Thy [G7] breast,
[C] Shelter me [F] safe in that [C] haven of [G7] rest,
[C] Shelter me [F] safe in that [C] haven of [G7] [C] rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Nearer, still nearer, [F] nothing I [C] bring,
Naught as an off'ring to [G7] Jesus my [C] King;
Only my [F] sinful, [C] now contrite [G7] heart,
[C] Grant me the [F] cleansing Thy [C] blood doth im-[G7] part,
[C] Grant me the [F] cleansing Thy [C] blood doth im-[G7] [C] part.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Nearer, still nearer, [F] Lord, to be [C] Thine,
Sin, with its follies, I [G7] gladly re-[C] sign;
All of its [F] pleasures, [C] pomp and its [G7] pride,
[C] Give me but [F] Jesus, my [C] Lord cruci-[G7] fied,
[C] Give me but [F] Jesus, my [C] Lord cruci-[G7] [C] fied.
{end_of_verse}
